BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Next Gen Brattleboro Launch
DTSTART:20261028T173000
DTEND:20261028T190000
DTSTAMP:20261028T171251Z
UID:a635e994449c060f2e0aa4ea2ed927@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:WHAT: A free\, open-to-all gathering of Greater Brattleboro re
 sidents to craft a shared future together and begin a sustained effort tow
 ards enacting it. WHY: Brattleboro faces demographic and economic headwind
 s. Communities across Vermont and New England are grappling with similar c
 hallenges and the status quo is not sustainable. A unified\, informed\, an
 d committed effort toward the long-term economic health and resilience of 
 the Greater Brattleboro community is required to remain affordable and att
 ractive. Fortunately\, Brattleboro is in a position of strength: we are on
 e of New England’s most extraordinary and magnetic small towns. Our natu
 ral beauty\, creative energy\, civic engagement\, deep sense of place\, an
 d thriving economy compel longtime residents and newcomers alike to choose
  to make a home here in our amazing community. WHO: Leaders from The Vermo
 nt Futures Project\, Next Gen Brattleboro and the community of Greater Bra
 ttleboro. Featuring Kevin Chu\, Executive Director of the Vermont Futures 
 Project\, a nonpartisan organization answering the mission question: “Ho
 w can we use data to support the evolution of Vermont’s economy towards 
 a thriving future with opportunity for all?” Chu’s work has taken him 
 all over the state to develop an Economic Action Plan\, helping to put Ver
 mont on a path towards affordability and abundance. Next Gen Brattleboro i
 s a civic alliance of organizations\, businesses\, community leaders\, and
  residents committed to Brattleboro’s long-term economic and community v
 itality and to building a broad movement to make Brattleboro a vibrant and
  affordable community for the next generation. The alliance will\, among o
 ther efforts\, champion the funding and implementation of catalyst project
 s to transform the town\, and are committed to taking concrete actions tha
 t strengthen this region. Special guests and local leaders will share prog
 ress\, plans and exciting “wins” since the group’s gathering at the 
 Retreat Farm in March and invite the community of Greater Brattleboro - lo
 ngtime residents\, local business owners\, new arrivals\, or simply anyone
  who cares about where Brattleboro is headed - to join them in sustained e
 ffort.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:The Latchis Theater\, 50 Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/next-gen-b
 rattleboro-launch-28-09-2026-10-54-10
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Oct 28 | Brave Little State at The Miller's Toll
DTSTART:20261028T173000
DTEND:20261028T193000
DTSTAMP:20261028T171251Z
UID:40092c669052f127d34a851fe5a826@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Brave Little State \, our people-powered show\, on Octobe
 r 28 in Bennington to mingle with fellow listeners and choose a topic for 
 a future episode. Take part in a live voting round and pick up some Brave 
 Little State merch to show off your fan status. Don’t forget to bring yo
 ur burning questions about Vermont\, the show or how our stories get made.
  Tickets are $10 and support Brave Little State and Vermont Public. The fi
 rst 75 attendees will receive a vintage Lawson’s Brave Little State Pale
  Ale pint glass. Click here to reserve your tickets . If space allows\, ti
 ckets will be available at the door. This event is made possible with supp
 ort from Heritage Family Credit Union . Schedule 5:30 p.m. - Event begins 
 | Food and drink available for purchase 5:45 p.m. - Welcome | Question sub
 missions begin 6:30 p.m. - Question submission ends | Voting round begins 
 7:00 p.m. - Voting round ends | Winners are announced 7:30 p.m. - Event en
 ds Accommodations Vermont Public is committed to providing access and acco
 mmodation for individuals with disabilities at our events. To request acco
 mmodations\, please email events@vermontpublic.org or call us at 802-655-9
 451 at least seven days in advance of the event. Cancellation Policy Pleas
 e let us know by emailing events@vermontpublic.org if you are not able to 
 join us so that we may release your tickets to someone else. If tickets ar
 e able to be resold\, we are happy to offer a refund\, minus the processin
 g fees. Directions and Parking The Miller’s Toll is located at 716 Main 
 St\, Bennington\, VT 05201 . Parking is available along Main Street/Rt. 9.
  Other questions? Email us at events@vermontpublic.org .\n\nSources: Vermo
 nt Public
LOCATION:The Miller's Toll Dinner Club & Lounge\, 726 Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/oct-28-bra
 ve-litte-state-at-the-millers-toll-01-09-2026-15-37-24
END:VEVENT
