BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Two Tents
DTSTART:20261101T190000
DTEND:20261101T210000
DTSTAMP:20261028T171251Z
UID:304a919093f4d259b8b0fda15f1343@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:As part of its 125th anniversary celebrations\, the Haskell Fr
 ee Library and Opera House presents a new comedy by Stanstead\, Quebec\, p
 laywright Ross Murray. The play is a fundraiser to support the infrastruct
 ure needs of the beloved cross-border institution. Two Tents will run Octo
 ber 23\, 24\, 30\, and 31 at 7 pm and October 25 and November 1 at 2 pm at
  the Haskell Opera House. Two Tents opens on Melanie and her husband Jim s
 etting up their tent on a campground\, only to discover that the man in th
 e adjacent site is Melanie’s long- ago ex\, Dale\, camping with his much
  younger girlfriend Nancy. When it's revealed that Dale is not there entir
 ely by accident\, secrets from the past threaten to blow up both relations
 hips. It’s a poignant comedy about broken hearts\, mid-life regrets\, an
 d the perils of love and the great outdoors. The cast of four consists of 
 Sarah Hardin (Newport)\, Mic Hallinan (Derby Line)\, Holly Lillis (Newport
  Center)\, and Benj Tabah (Lennoxville). Ross Murray directs his own scrip
 t. The Haskell Library has undergone a major transformation in the past ye
 ar. When new border restrictions banned Canadian patrons from entering the
  library via the US front door\, library trustees were able to convert a f
 ire exit into a proper entrance on the Canadian side\, thanks to many dona
 tions from its supporter. But the 125- year-old building has many ongoing 
 infrastructure and maintenance needs that likewise require generous suppor
 t. Attending Two Tents is an opportunity to help preserve and enrich this 
 cherished cultural landmark. In addition to a night of heartfelt comedy\, 
 the production will also feature one of the Haskell Opera House’s rarely
  seen original painted backdrops. Note that Two Tents contains mature subj
 ects and mild language\; recommended 13 plus. Artist Group Info Ross Murra
 y rossgrantmurray@gmail.com 93 Caswell Ave Derby Line \, Vermont 05830 Sub
 mit An Event Find out what's happening in your neck of the woods with Verm
 ont Public's free Events newsletter. Email Address * Editorial Emails Brea
 king News | sent occasionally The Frequency | Daily News Update\, sent wee
 kday mornings Capitol Recap | Vermont Legislature Wrap\, sent Fridays duri
 ng the session Brave Little State | People-Powered Journalism\, sent every
  other Saturday But Why | A Podcast For Curious Kids\, sent every other Fr
 iday Homegoings | A righteous space for art and race\, sent bi-weekly foll
 owing an episode drop Out There | Out There | Your monthly dose of the env
 ironment + the great outdoors\, sent Thursday mor Supporter Emails Members
 hip Renewal Notices | Sent 12 months after your most recent contribution T
 he President's Report | A letter from our president exclusively for member
 s of our Producers Circle The Transmitter | A behind-the-scenes newsletter
  exclusively for active members\, sent the first Tues But Why Fan Club | A
 ctivity Newsletter exclusively for active members of the But Why Fan Club
 \, sent Other Fundraising Emails | Matching challenges\, prize drawings an
 d more\, sent periodically Audience Emails Program Schedules | Full TV lis
 tings for all channels\, sent monthly This Week | Weekly program highlight
 s\, sent each weekend Events | Upcoming Vermont Public events\, sent occas
 ionally Station Updates | Sent occasionally Recently Added Coat Giveaway C
 rowdsourced Cinema VT Film Screening – SHREK! Bella Voce “Cool Yule!
 ” Holiday Concerts Katarina String Quartet Stay Connected twitter instag
 ram youtube bluesky facebook Vermont Public is independent\, community-sup
 ported media\, serving Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential infor
 mation. We share stories that bring people together\, from every corner of
  our region. © 2026 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446 
 Public Files: WVTI · WOXM · WVBA · WVNK · WVTQ WVPR · WRVT · WOXR ·
  WNCH · WVPA WVPS · WVXR · WETK · WVTB · WVER WVER-FM · WVLR-FM · W
 BTN-FM For assistance accessing our public files\, please contact hello@ve
 rmontpublic.org or call 802-655-9451. ABOUT About Us Announcements Our Tea
 m Board of Directors Community Forum Careers & Internships Vermont Public 
 in Canada POLICIES & REPORTS Privacy Policy Ethics\, Editorial and Other P
 olicies EEO Reports & Statement FCC Applications Financial Information Con
 test Rules SUPPORT US Donate Now Update Membership Philanthropy Legacy Giv
 ing Business Sponsorship Donate Your Car Vermont Public Passport\n\nSource
 s: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Haskell Free Library and Opera House
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/two-tents-
 05-10-2026-11-21-30
END:VEVENT
